  "inputContract": "Catalog SKU-00000..09999; price cents=1000+(id*37)%100000. Import row i uses missing key if i%17=0 else SKU-(i*7919)%10000; quantity=i%5+1. Output is price*quantity or -1 for missing.",
  "outputContract": "SHA-256 of every output as signed little-endian 64-bit integer, plus count/missing/sum; independently verified in Python for every warmup and measured run",
  "metricScope": "End-to-end import includes building a new index and allocating output array for every batch. Input creation and output hashing are outside every arm. CPU and allocations measured over same operation. No network/delay injected.",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic import, not a migrated customer application",
    "All arms use the same .NET10 runtime; no .NET Framework versus10 or version-only speed claim",
    "Dictionary is available on older .NET versions; improvement is algorithm/data-structure choice",
    "FrozenDictionary construction overhead is included and all controls retained even if slower",
    "Managed allocated bytes are cumulative allocation during operation, not peak memory/RSS or a monetary saving",
    "Shared Apple host, Docker VM and1CPUquota; no claim of production-machine isolation",
    "Two warmups per point, tiered compilation disabled; startup and long-term JIT behavior excluded",
    "No security, web request, database, or cloud-bill improvement measured"
